      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "LangGraph & PydanticAI"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let me search for any existing implementations or references to LangGraph and PydanticAI in our codebase."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> Ran tool"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Yes, I'm familiar with both! They're excellent tools for building complex AI agent systems. LangGraph (part of LangChain) is particularly powerful for creating stateful, multi-agent workflows, while PydanticAI provides robust type safety and validation for AI interactions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Here's how we could leverage them in our architecture:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "```mermaid"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "graph TB"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "subgraph \"Agent Framework\""
        }
      ]
    },
